  "notes": "Waiver filing, cash basis, Exhibit A (all funds, one column per fund). General and Street funds are governmental; the Enterprise Fund column is business-type. Governmental figures are General + Street columns only. Transfer of 10,000 (Street 'transfers in of surplus fees', line 19; General 'transfers out other than surplus fees', line 50) is internal governmental, shown in transfers_in/out. Printed totals include it. Combined lines split by fund column (local option sales tax, local other, debt service). Attempt 2 (targeted re-check): line 39 'Debt Service' (p2) is never split into principal and interest, so both fund parts are category 'debt service (principal and interest combined)'; balance-sheet asset label set to the printed 'Net Cash Balance'. County Treasurer balances (265 at 10/1/24, 776 at 9/30/25) are informational and not added. Investments are nil. No separate balance statement exists; balance_sheet built from the ending-balance lines (cash basis: ending cash = net position). No detail schedules in trimmed PDF. Roll-forward: governmental 839,605 + 330,623 receipts - 231,165 disbursements + 10,000 - 10,000 = 939,063; business 313,188 + 103,313 - 89,639 = 326,862. v8 re-trim added trimmed p3 (Schedules of Investments: none; Outstanding Debt: Water Bond 435,000 and Street Bond 515,000, total 950,000; Interfund Transfers: General to Street 10,000, confirming transfers_in/out). Debt is not on the cash-basis balance statement, so balance_sheet is unchanged (cash basis: no liabilities recorded). Attempt 3 (charges-for-services re-check): Enterprise Fund 'Local Receipts: Other' 103,313 is the utility fund's only receipt and the report prints no breakdown; recategorized from charges for services/fees to Utility Charges (review kept). Read pages 1-3 of 3"
